  <Prose
    title="Licence"
    standfirst="GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later. Free to use, free to read, free to change — and a hosted version has to stay that way too."
    updated="18 August 2026"
  >
    <h2>What you may do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use it, for anything, including commercially.</li>
      <li>Read all of it, and change any of it.</li>
      <li>Share it, and share your changes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      What you must do in return: keep it under the same licence, say what you changed, and
      pass the source on with the software. And the clause the Affero licence adds — if you run
      a modified version as a network service, the people using it must be able to get its
      source.
    </p>

    <h2>Why this licence and not a permissive one</h2>
    <p>
      Sync and hosted backup are planned, and they would be paid. Under the ordinary GPL,
      running a modified version as a service is not distribution, so a closed hosted fork of
      this project would be perfectly legal. The Affero clause is the difference, and it is the
      whole reason for choosing it here.
    </p>
    <p>
      It has a cost, recorded here rather than discovered later: Apple's App Store terms
      conflict with the (A)GPL, so an AGPL-only iOS build could not be distributed there. There
      is no iOS build today, and the copyright sits in one place, so that path stays open to be
      reconsidered.
    </p>

    <h2>The material this project bundles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Archivo</strong>, the typeface this site is set in — SIL Open Font License 1.1.
        Served from this domain, never from anyone else's.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Lucide</strong> icons — ISC.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Vue, Vite, Pinia, Pinia Colada, Astro, Capacitor, Tailwind CSS</strong> — MIT,
        except where each project states otherwise.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Every screenshot on this site is of this application, captured automatically against its
      own bundled demo data. No stock imagery is used anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>The text itself</h2>
    <p>
      The complete licence is in the repository as
      <a href="https://github.com/yebt/some-kaizen/blob/main/LICENSE" rel="noopener">LICENSE</a>,
      with the reasoning and the third-party list in
      <a href="https://github.com/yebt/some-kaizen/blob/main/NOTICE.md" rel="noopener">NOTICE.md</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
